  "triggers": [
    {
      "id": "gallery_enter",
      "event": "room_entered",
      "actions": [
        { "type": "showMessage", "lines": [
          "The passage opens into a long, vaulted gallery. Every surface is covered in murals carved directly into the stone — geometric patterns that seem to shift in the faint ambient light.",
          "Wind whispers through channels cut into the gallery walls, creating a low harmonic that resonates in your chest. The murals aren't just decorative. They're functional — part of the wind-generation system.",
          "This was a place of record. Whatever civilization built the Spires, they left their history here, encoded in stone and wind."
        ]}
      ],
      "once": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mural_civilization",
      "event": "room_entered",
      "conditions": [{ "not": { "hasFlag": "gallery_mural_1" } }],
      "actions": [
        { "type": "setFlag", "flag": "gallery_mural_1" },
        { "type": "showMessage", "lines": [
          "A large mural panel depicts a network of towering structures — Spires, dozens of them — connected by lines of energy that arc across a landscape unrecognizable as modern terrain.",
          "The civilization that built these Spires operated on a continental scale. The Monument of Winds was just one node in a vast network. Your sol unit pulses in recognition."
        ]},
        { "type": "grantXp", "amount": 15 }
      ],
      "once": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mural_wind_architecture",
      "event": "room_entered",
      "conditions": [
        { "hasFlag": "gallery_mural_1" },
        { "not": { "hasFlag": "gallery_mural_2" } }
      ],
      "actions": [
        { "type": "setFlag", "flag": "gallery_mural_2" },
        { "type": "showMessage", "lines": [
          "Another mural sequence shows the construction of the Monument itself. Figures — not human, but humanoid — direct flows of energy that lift stone into place without physical contact.",
          "The wind wasn't a byproduct of the architecture. The architecture was built to generate and channel wind. The entire Monument is a machine for moving air in precise patterns."
        ]},
        { "type": "grantXp", "amount": 15 }
      ],
      "once": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mural_collapse",
      "event": "room_entered",
      "conditions": [
        { "hasFlag": "gallery_mural_2" },
        { "not": { "hasFlag": "gallery_mural_3" } }
      ],
      "actions": [
        { "type": "setFlag", "flag": "gallery_mural_3" },
        { "type": "showMessage", "lines": [
          "The final mural is damaged — partially erased by time or intent. What remains shows the Spire network going dark, one node at a time. The connecting lines of energy fracturing and fading.",
          "Something ended this civilization. Not suddenly, but progressively — a slow failure cascading through their network. The Spires were their last attempt to preserve something. But what?"
        ]},
        { "type": "grantXp", "amount": 20 }
      ],
      "once": true
    }
  ]
